## Summary

### 1. The computation function

**`RebuildMemoPayload`** — `/bench/repo/server/runner/memopayload/runner.go:74-88`

```go
func RebuildMemoPayload(_ context.Context, memo *store.Memo, markdownService markdown.Service) error {
	if memo.Payload == nil {
		memo.Payload = &storepb.MemoPayload{}
	}
	// Use goldmark service to extract all metadata in a single pass (more efficient)
	data, err := markdownService.ExtractAll([]byte(memo.Content))
	if err != nil {
		return errors.Wrap(err, "failed to extract markdown metadata")
	}
	memo.Payload.Tags = data.Tags
	memo.Payload.Property = data.Property
	return nil
}
```

It is in package `server/runner/memopayload` (not `internal/markdown`). It delegates the actual extraction to `markdown.Service.ExtractAll` (interface at `/bench/repo/internal/markdown/markdown.go:33`, implementation `/bench/repo/internal/markdown/markdown.go:356-422`), which does a single AST walk to populate an `ExtractedData{Tags, Mentions, Property}` struct (`markdown.go:20-25`).

### 2. Call sites of `RebuildMemoPayload`

| File:Line | Enclosing handler | Trigger |
|---|---|---|
| `/bench/repo/server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:108` | `func (s *APIV1Service) CreateMemo(...)` (starts line 70) | `CreateMemo` RPC — rebuilds payload right after the new `store.Memo` struct is assembled, before `s.Store.CreateMemo` persists it |
| `/bench/repo/server/router/api/v1/memo_service.go:447` | `func (s *APIV1Service) UpdateMemo(...)` (starts line 401) | `UpdateMemo` RPC — only when `request.UpdateMask.Paths` contains `"content"` (inside the `for _, path := range request.UpdateMask.Paths { if path == "content" { ... } }` branch); it's what triggers `update.Payload = memo.Payload` for the DB update |
| `/bench/repo/server/runner/memopayload/runner.go:52` | `func (r *Runner) RunOnce(ctx context.Context)` | Background maintenance runner, not an RPC handler — iterates over all memos in batches and rebuilds/persists every memo's payload (used e.g. after a markdown-extraction logic change / migration) |

No other RPC handler in `server/router/api/v1/*.go` calls `RebuildMemoPayload` — in particular there is no tag-rename RPC that triggers it (a repo-wide grep for `RenameTag`/`RenameMemoTag` under `server/router/api/v1` returned nothing; `RenameTag` only exists as a markdown-service method at `internal/markdown/markdown.go:425` used to rewrite tag text in content, not to recompute payload metadata).

Two other, unrelated call sites use markdown-extraction methods directly for different purposes (not full payload rebuild, and not persisted to `MemoPayload`):
- `/bench/repo/server/router/api/v1/memo_mention_helpers.go:32` — `resolveMentionTargets` calls `s.MarkdownService.ExtractAll` just to pull out `@mentions` for notification purposes.
- `/bench/repo/server/router/api/v1/memo_service_webhooks.go:85` — `getMemoContentSnippet` calls `s.MarkdownService.GenerateSnippet(content, 64)` to build a transient snippet for outgoing webhook payloads (not stored in `MemoPayload`).

### 3. Extracted/derived properties stored in `MemoPayload`

Proto source: `/bench/repo/proto/store/memo.proto` (generated Go: `/bench/repo/proto/gen/store/memo.pb.go:24-30, 85-93`)

```proto
message MemoPayload {
  Property property = 1;
  Location location = 2;
  repeated string tags = 3;

  message Property {
    bool has_link = 1;
    bool has_task_list = 2;
    bool has_code = 3;
    bool has_incomplete_tasks = 4;
    string title = 5;   // extracted from the first H1 heading, if present
  }

  message Location {
    string placeholder = 1;
    double latitude = 2;
    double longitude = 3;
  }
}
```

Fields set by `RebuildMemoPayload`/`ExtractAll` (from `internal/markdown/markdown.go:356-422`, mirrored in `ExtractProperties` at lines 192-241):
- `Payload.Tags` (`[]string`) — all `#tag` nodes found via AST walk (`mast.TagNode`), deduplicated case-preserving.
- `Payload.Property.HasLink` (`bool`) — true if any `gast.KindLink` node present.
- `Payload.Property.HasCode` (`bool`) — true if any `KindCodeBlock`, `KindFencedCodeBlock`, or `KindCodeSpan` node present.
- `Payload.Property.HasTaskList` (`bool`) — true if any `east.KindTaskCheckBox` node present.
- `Payload.Property.HasIncompleteTasks` (`bool`) — true if any task checkbox is unchecked.
- `Payload.Property.Title` (`string`) — text of the first block-level child of the document if it's an H1 heading (extracted via `extractHeadingText`).

Note: `Location` is **not** derived from content — it's set separately from the request in `CreateMemo` (`memo_service.go:110-112`, `convertLocationToStore(request.Memo.Location)`), it's direct user input, not computed markdown metadata.

Also note: `Snippet`/preview text is **not** part of the persisted `MemoPayload` proto at all — `GenerateSnippet` (markdown.go:264-346) exists but is only used transiently for webhook dispatch (`memo_service_webhooks.go:83-90`), not stored via `RebuildMemoPayload`. Similarly, `Mentions` (`ExtractedData.Mentions`) is computed by `ExtractAll` but is discarded by `RebuildMemoPayload` (only `.Tags` and `.Property` are copied to `memo.Payload`) — mentions are instead re-extracted independently by `resolveMentionTargets` for notification purposes.
